==English==
[[File:06 Restoration of gilded mirror in Muzeum Gornoslaskie, Bytom, Poland - furniture restorer working.jpg|thumb|right|The '''restoration''' ({{senseno|en|process}}) of antique mirror involved repainting its frame.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|restauration}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|restaurātiō}}. {{surf|en|restore|-ation}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɛstəˈɹeɪʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-restoration.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|re|sto|ra|tion}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|process}} The process of bringing an object back to its [[original]] [[state]]; the process of [[restore|restoring]] something.
#: {{synonyms|en|restitution}}
#: {{ux|en|[[foreskin]] '''restoration'''}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of this painting will take years.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of this medieval church involved undoing all the Victorian modifications.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1921|author=w:T.S. Eliot|title=The Sacred Wood|chapter=The Possibility of a Poetic Drama
|passage=There is all the difference between preservation and '''restoration'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1945|month=July and August|title=Victory in Europe|journal=Railway Magazine|page=187|text=As Sir Ronald Matthews said at the meeting of L.N.E.R. stockholders earlier this year, the public must realise "the inevitability of a certain amount of gradualness" in connection with the '''restoration''' of passenger train services and facilities.}}
# The [[return]] of a [[former]] [[monarchy]] or [[monarch]] to [[power]], usually after having been forced to step down.
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of the House of Stuart took place a few years after the death of Cromwell.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''restoration''' of the Kingdom of Spain took place immediately after the death of Franco.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Albion and Albanius|act=I|scene=i|page=10|passage=Behold the differing Climes agree, / Rejoycing in thy '''Reſtauration'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2024/01/trump-reelection-mental-health-psychological-impact/676142/|title=What Will Happen to the American Psyche If Trump Is Reelected?|work=The Atlantic|date=2023-12-08|author=w:Jennifer Senior|passage=But now here we are, faced with the prospect of a Trump '''restoration'''.}}
# {{lb|en|theology}} The [[receive|receiving]] of a [[sinner]] to [[divine]] [[favor]].

